userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: Because a point on the unit circle moves continuously with its angle, letting x approach c forces P(cos x, sin x) to approach Q(cos c, sin c), which geometrically establishes lim_{x->c} sin x = sin c and lim_{x->c} cos x = cos c, i.e. sine and cosine are continuous at every c.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Continuity of sine and cosine is just the fact that the point (cos x, sin x) slides continuously around the unit circle as the angle x varies, so x -> c forces the coordinates to approach (cos c, sin c) from both sides.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

